SUMMARY:🐟Walk:  Salmon Run at Humber River & James Gardens 🍂
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🐟 Salmon Run at Humber River 
 & James Gardens 🍂\n\n### An Easy Fall Walk — With a Pretty Amazing Na
 tural Show Along the Way\n\nEvery fall\, something incredible happens righ
 t here in Toronto.\nSalmon make their way upstream through the **Humber Ri
 ver**\, battling rapids and leaping through the water as they return to fr
 eshwater to spawn.\nAnd yes — you can actually see them doing it.\n\nJoi
 n us for a relaxed\, social walk along the Humber River during salmon run 
 season. We'll spend about 30 minutes by the river watching for salmon befo
 re continuing along the trail toward **James Gardens**.\nThis isn't a diff
 icult hike. It's a chance to get outside\, enjoy the fall scenery\, see so
 mething you might not normally experience in the city\, and spend some tim
 e with other people along the way.\n\n✨ **Fun Fact:** Some salmon travel
  more than 3\,000 km from the Atlantic Ocean to reach freshwater rivers li
 ke the Humber. After all that distance\, they still have to battle rapids 
 and leap over obstacles to reach their spawning grounds.\nNature really do
 esn't mess around.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [
 CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n
 ## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll begin outside the station and make
  our way toward the Humber River.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Walk along th
 e Humber River\n* Stop for approximately 30 minutes to look for salmon\n* 
 Watch the salmon making their way upstream\n* Continue along the river tow
 ard James Gardens\n* Take a break at **James Gardens**\n* Enjoy the fall s
 cenery and take some photos\n* Make our way back toward the station\n\nThe
  walk is approximately **90 minutes**\, depending on the pace of the group
  and how long we spend watching the salmon.\nAnd remember — **the salmon
  are wild animals.** We can't guarantee exactly how many we'll see\, or ho
 w long they'll put on a show. That's part of the fun!\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 Wh
 y Come?\n\nThe salmon run is one of those strange little Toronto experienc
 es that you can easily miss if you don't know when and where to look.\nOne
  minute you're walking through the city. The next\, you're standing beside
  a river watching salmon fight their way upstream.\nWe'll also visit **Jam
 es Gardens**\, one of those beautiful green spaces that can make you forge
 t you're still in Toronto.\nBring your camera\, bring your curiosity\, and
  come see what the Humber has to offer in the fall.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ We
 ather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place outdoors in typical Toronto 
 fall weather.\nPlease dress appropriately for the conditions and wear comf
 ortable walking shoes. The trail may be damp or muddy depending on recent 
 weather.\nBring water and a snack\, and dress in layers — fall weather c
 an change quickly.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Locat
 ion:** Right outside the station\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n
 ⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is
  on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Back at the station\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 *
 *mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows 
 us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 Wha
 t to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n
 🧴 Sunscreen if it's sunny\n📷 A camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n
 ## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* Anyone who wants 
 an easy fall outing\n* People who enjoy nature and wildlife\n* Anyone curi
 ous about Toronto's rivers and green spaces\n* People looking for a relaxe
 d social walk\n* Anyone who wants to meet new people while exploring the c
 ity\n* Salmon enthusiasts — obviously. 🐟\n\nThe activity is the conta
 iner. **The people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\n**
 *\n\n📲 **REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show 
 up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happ
 en and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye 
 on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? P
 ost on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.co
 m**\n\n**Come for the salmon.**\n**Stay for the walk.**\n**Leave with a ne
 w connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
