SUMMARY:Fall Walk: From Cabbagetown to Cherry Street 🌿 🍺
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂 Fall Walk: From Rosedale to
  Cherry Street 🌿\n\n### A Fall Walk Through Some of Toronto's Most Inte
 resting Neighbourhoods\n\nLooking for a walk that gives you a little bit o
 f everything?\nWe'll start in **Rosedale**\, make our way through **Cabbag
 etown and Regent Park**\, wander through the **Distillery District**\, sto
 p at **Biidaasige Park**\, and finish with a well-earned meal at **Cherry 
 Street Bar-B-Que**.\nAlong the way\, we'll see some of the city's oldest n
 eighbourhoods\, newer communities\, historic architecture\, green spaces\,
  and some pretty great views.\nIt's a longer walk\, but the route is more 
 about **exploring Toronto together** than trying to finish as quickly as p
 ossible.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE
 ](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍
 ♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet outside **Rosedale Station** and begin 
 our walk through Rosedale Valley\, following the tree-lined route toward C
 abbagetown.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Walk through Rosedale Valley 🌳\n
 * Explore the historic streets of Cabbagetown\n* Pass through Regent Park\
 n* Wander through the Distillery District\n* Stop at Biidaasige Park\n* Ta
 ke in the fall scenery and city views\n* Finish at **Cherry Street Bar-B-Q
 ue** 🍖\n\nThe walk includes a **long set of stairs**\, so while this is
 n't a difficult hike\, you should be comfortable walking for several hours
  and keeping up with the group.\n\n***\n\n## 🏙️ A Little Toronto Hist
 ory Along the Way\n\nThis walk takes us through several very different par
 ts of Toronto.\nIn **Cabbagetown**\, we'll pass beautifully preserved Vict
 orian homes and streets that reflect the neighbourhood's long history\, in
 cluding its Irish roots.\n\nWe'll then make our way through **Regent Park*
 *\, one of Toronto's most historically significant communities\, where old
 er social housing has been joined by new housing\, arts\, and community sp
 aces.\nFrom there\, we'll head into the **Distillery District**\, with its
  cobblestone streets and historic red-brick buildings.\n\nWe'll also stop 
 at **Biidaasige Park**\, whose name means *“the sun is shining”* in An
 ishinaabemowin.\nIt's a lot of Toronto in one walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🍺 The 
 Keating Channel Pub & Grill\n\nWe'll finish our walk at **The Keating Chan
 nel Pub & Grill**\, right on the Keating Channel.\n\nThere's a bit of hist
 ory behind this stop. The pub struggled during the massive Port Lands cons
 truction\, when road closures and the relocation of the Cherry Street brid
 ge made the area difficult to reach. With the Port Lands now transformed a
 nd **Biidaasige Park** open\, people are rediscovering this part of the ci
 ty — and the pub is getting a second chance.\n\nAfter exploring the new 
 park and the transformed Port Lands\, we'll finish at one of the neighbour
 hood's old survivors: a casual waterfront pub with a patio overlooking the
  Keating Channel.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is a 
 **long urban walk**\, not a difficult hike\, but you should be comfortable
  being on your feet for several hours.\nThere is a long set of stairs alon
 g the route.\nPlease wear comfortable walking shoes and dress appropriatel
 y for the weather.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Locat
 ion:** Outside Rosedale Station\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n
 ⏰ **Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM sharp\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Ea
 rly is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Cherry Street Bar-
 B-Que\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer
 **\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group a
 nd allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n#
 # 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A
  snack\n🧴 Sunscreen\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n\n***\n\n## 
 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy exp
 loring Toronto\n* Anyone who likes history and architecture\n* People look
 ing for a longer social walk\n* Anyone who wants to discover neighbourhood
 s they might not normally visit\n* People who enjoy stopping for food at t
 he end\n* Anyone who wants to spend a Sunday exploring the city with other
  people\n\nThe destination isn't really the point.\n**It's the people you 
 meet along the way.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show
  up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things hap
 pen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye
  on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? 
 Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n
 \n**Come for the walk.**\n**Stay for the friendship.**\n**And maybe stay a
  little longer for lunch.** 🍺🌿
