SUMMARY:🌙🍂 Fall Evening Walk: High Park & Ghost Stories 👻
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌙🍂 **Fall Evening Walk: Hi
 gh Park & Ghost Stories** 👻\n\n### Fall Colours\, Spooky Stories & A Di
 fferent Way to Spend Your Evening\n\nLooking for something a little differ
 ent to do after work?\n\nJoin us for an **evening walk through High Park**
 \, where we'll enjoy the fall colours while stopping along the way for som
 e of the park's stranger\, spookier\, and downright weird stories.\nHigh P
 ark has a long history of ghost stories and local legends.\n\nFrom stories
  connected to the **War of 1812** — yes\, *that* War of 1812 — to tale
 s of mysterious deaths and people who may not have completely left the par
 k behind\, there's plenty of history to make an ordinary fall walk a littl
 e more interesting.\nBut don't worry.\n\n**This isn't a terrifying ghost h
 unt.** 👻\n\nThink **fall colours\, creepy stories\, a little history\, 
 a few laughs\, and just enough spooky atmosphere to make you look over you
 r shoulder once or twice.**\n\nIt's a relaxed way to get outside after wor
 k\, explore one of Toronto's most beautiful parks\, and experience High Pa
 rk as the daylight starts to disappear. 🍂🌙\n\n📱 Don't forget to j
 oin our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSC
 bsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll walk through 
 **High Park**\, stopping at different locations along the way while I shar
 e stories connected to the park's history and ghostly legends.\nAlong the 
 way we'll:\n\n* Explore some of High Park's most interesting locations\n* 
 Hear stories of ghosts\, legends\, and strange events 👻\n* Learn a litt
 le about the park's history\n* Take photos and enjoy the scenery 📸\n* H
 ave some Halloween fun along the way 🎃\n\nWe'll keep a steady walking p
 ace\, with regular stops for storytelling.\nThe walk will remain **outside
  throughout** — there is no entry into buildings.\n\n***\n\n## 🎃 Hall
 oween Day — So Let's Have Some Fun\n\nThis isn't meant to be a serious p
 aranormal investigation.\n\nSome stories are creepy. Some are strange. Som
 e might make you wonder whether there's actually something going on.\nAnd 
 some are just a good excuse to tell a spooky story while walking through t
 he fall leaves.\n\n**You don't have to believe in ghosts.**\nYou just have
  to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nT
 his is an outdoor walk\, so please dress appropriately for the weather.\nH
 igh Park can be cool and damp in late October\, so bring a warm jacket and
  wear comfortable walking shoes.\nWe'll be walking at a steady pace\, with
  stops along the way for stories and photos.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Deta
 ils\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** High Park sign on the west side at Bloor 
 Street West & High Park Avenue\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰
  **Meetup Time:** **6:30pm sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Ear
 ly is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶 **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n
 🏁 **End Point:** Back where we started\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\
 n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com*
 *\nThis is a **curated\, guided storytelling experience**\, rather than on
 e of our regular group walks. The route\, stories\, and history have been 
 researched and developed specifically for this experience.\n\n***\n\n## 
 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 War
 m fall jacket or layers\n📸 Camera or phone\n🎃 Halloween spirit\nAnd 
 if you want to wear a costume...\n**I'm certainly not going to stop you.**
  👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great for:\n\n* People
  who love Halloween 🎃\n* Anyone who enjoys ghost stories\n* Fall-colour
  enthusiasts 🍂\n* History buffs\n* People looking for something differe
 nt to do on Halloween Day\n* Anyone who enjoys a good story and a few laug
 hs\n* People who want to meet new people while exploring Toronto\n\nYou're
  welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure
  about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be c
 ancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.
 \n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email
  **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the fall colours.**
  🍂\n**Stay for the ghost stories.** 👻\n**Leave with a new connection
  — if the ghosts don't get you first.** 🎃
