SUMMARY:🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris T
 rail 🌳🍂\n\n### A Hidden Ravine\, Easy Walking & Great Conversation\n
 \nSometimes the best parts of Toronto are the ones most people drive right
  past.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed fall walk along the **Gus Harris Trail**\,
  a quiet ravine trail that follows **Taylor-Massey Creek** through Scarbor
 ough and East York.\n\nThis isn't a challenging hike. It's an easy\, mostl
 y flat walk through one of Toronto's quieter green spaces\, with plenty of
  time to enjoy the changing leaves\, get some fresh air\, and meet other p
 eople along the way.\n\nWe'll follow the creek\, walk beneath the trees\, 
 and take our time enjoying the fall scenery.\nThe goal isn't to race to th
 e end of the trail. **It's to get outside\, have some good conversations\,
  and enjoy the company.**\n\n✨ **Fun Fact:** Taylor-Massey Creek takes i
 ts name from two prominent Toronto families. The Taylor family was associa
 ted with the Don Valley Brick Works\, now home to Evergreen Brick Works.\n
 \n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://
 chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ Wha
 t We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend about **two hours** walking along the trail\, ta
 king our time\, chatting\, and getting to know one another.\nThis is a **s
 ocial walk\, not a race.**\n\nThe route has very few hills\, making it a c
 omfortable walk for most people with a reasonable level of fitness.\nWe'll
  finish back where we started.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectatio
 ns\n\nThis walk takes place outdoors in typical Toronto fall weather.\nPle
 ase dress appropriately for the conditions and wear comfortable walking sh
 oes. The trail may be damp or muddy depending on recent weather.\nBring wa
 ter and a snack\, and dress in layers if the temperature is changing throu
 ghout the day.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:
 ** Outside Victoria Park Subway Station\, by Victoria Park Road.\n🫎 **L
 ook for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will
  only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **
 End Point:** Victoria Park Subway Station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\
 n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**
 \nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing ev
 ents throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n
 👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweate
 r\n🦟 Bug spray if needed\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis wal
 k is great for:\n\n* Anyone who enjoys fall scenery 🍂\n* People looking
  for an easy trail\n* Anyone who wants to get outside and get moving\n* Pe
 ople who enjoy exploring Toronto's hidden green spaces\n* Anyone looking f
 or a relaxed social outing\n* People who want to meet new people and make 
 friends\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day
  if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events
  may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event 
 page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the ev
 ent wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n\n**Come for t
 he trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection
  — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
